<BaseLayout title="About">
  <section class="page-intro"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow">About</span><h1>Grounded in operations. Led by service.</h1><p>Technology leadership for the people, production rhythms and business priorities of garment manufacturing in Myanmar.</p></div></section>
  <section class="container about-grid">
    <aside class="about-aside"><strong>Technology is a team sport.</strong><p>The best systems are the ones people can rely on, understand and use with confidence.</p></aside>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>I work at the intersection of IT operations and garment production. That means looking beyond uptime reports to understand what a technology decision means for a merchandiser, a finance team, a production planner or a line supervisor.</p>
      <p>My approach is practical: make the current environment visible, reduce avoidable risk, build trusted relationships and deliver improvements in stages. I value clear communication and repeatable operations as much as the technology itself.</p>
      <h2>What I bring</h2>
      <p>A broad IT management perspective across infrastructure, business systems, information security, service delivery, vendor relationships and team development, shaped for the realities of a manufacturing environment.</p>
      <div class="value-grid">
        <div class="value-item"><span>01</span><h3>Operational clarity</h3><p>Know what matters, who owns it and how to recover.</p></div>
        <div class="value-item"><span>02</span><h3>Measured change</h3><p>Prioritize outcomes and keep delivery understandable.</p></div>
        <div class="value-item"><span>03</span><h3>Shared ownership</h3><p>Build capability across IT and business teams.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>